From: MacFinals
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: fix the C04/C06 diagnostics (lock type, query direction, races)

Review of wine-macdrv-event-queue-lock.patch (macfinals-133) and
wine-macdrv-focus-rendezvous-log.patch (macfinals-135) found:

1. os_unfair_lock is NOT released when its owner dies (tested 2026-11-22: trylock stays
   busy forever, and a blocking lock aborts the process). So -133 turned "dead holder hangs
   the queue" into "dead holder crashes the game" on the Cocoa main thread's posting path.
   The queue lock is upstream's NSLock again (a dead holder hangs, as before; tryLock and
   lockBeforeDate time out cleanly - tested). The bounded 100 ms drain and the holder record
   stay; the "previous holder never released it" ERR is removed (unreachable: a blocking
   acquire of a dead holder's lock never returns, with either lock).
2. query: runs on the Cocoa main thread, which waits for the Wine thread that owns the
   window - the opposite of what -135 logged ("tid X waiting for main thread", with the
   main thread's own id, always 0000). It now records the main thread as waiter, the
   queue's owner thread (captured when the queue is created) as target, the query type by
   name, and the window's hwnd.
3. Holder/waiter ids were 0 for the Cocoa main thread and threads outside the syscall log,
   so a long hold by the main thread was never reported and skips said "tid 0000". They are
   now named "Cocoa main thread" / "unlogged thread" (macdrv_diag_self / macdrv_diag_who).
4. Waits and main-thread request execution use ntdll's per-wait registry instead of shared
   slots (one waiter's return no longer erases another's record; nested requests get their
   own entries).
5. Focus state: separate state lines with real ages; app state read from [NSApp isActive]
   (applicationDidBecomeActive: is also called by hand when the app may be inactive); key
   window by hwnd, and a resign only clears its own window (resign/become can arrive in
   either order). New: the game window's visibility (occlusion) and display sleep, screen
   saver and screen lock - the AFK case.
6. Trace lines lacked a newline (they ran together); OnMainThread is hot (SetCursorPos
   outside mouselook), so only waits over 20 ms trace. The diagnostics have their own
   channel, WINEDEBUG=+macfinals_ui, instead of +macdrv (which enables every macdrv trace).
7. The skipped-drain ERR is rate-limited to one a second with a skip count, and its hold
   time can no longer underflow.
